Job Title: Finance and Admin Manager
Location: Abuja, Nigeria
Reports to: Finance and Admin Director
Job Summary
The Finance and Admin Manager will manage and lead everyday financial activities including reporting. S/he will be responsible for providing financial guidance and support to clients/partners, colleagues, and management. In this role, s/he will develop tailored project budgets, prepare periodic financial reports and updates for internal and external parties as well as develop, implement, and review financial policies and procedures, and ensure compliance to all client/donor financial requirements.
Specific Responsibilities
Accounting and Treasury Management
Accounting management – supervise the accounting cycle:
Ensure timely and accurate data entries into QuickBooks following the standard descriptions defined in our Finance Procedure Manual;
Verify and coordinate the monthly finance records from each State offices;
Supervise cash and bank balance checking process when closing the monthly accounts;
Manage the presentation, circulation, filing of vouchers and archiving of accounting and financial documents in compliance with our Account and Finance procedures;
Supervise the Yearly and Quarterly Accounting Closures for both General and Analytical Accountancy aspects.
Treasury management – ensure a controlled and smooth cash management:
Ensure justified bank selection process, open/close bank accounts;
Oversee the management of bank accounts: control, follow and make sure flows are properly lettered (advances, transfers, etc.), check balances, etc;
Supervise the management of safes and cash: available amount, balance checks, security instructions;
Assess monthly cash-flow needs for projects and state offices;
Manage money transfers, areas cash-supply and amounts in circulation, whilst defining payment procedures (bank transfer, cheque, cash etc.);
Make sure donors are invoiced on time.
Manage relationship with the bankers.
Approve payments in line with defined authority limits.
Commitment Of Expenditures, Budget Control, & Financial Management
Commitment of expenditure – guaranty budget availability and compliance to internal and donor’s procedures before releasing payments:
Before commitment / payment of any expenditure, check authorization levels, budget availability, budget line on which the expense is to be allocated to, ensuring full compliance with internal and donors’ procedures:
In close coordination with the Logistics unit, negotiate terms of contracts including payment schedule and tax obligations; ensure that procurement procedures are adhered to;
Ensure financial, compliance and budget control points during Purchase Committee meetings; review coherence between orders, quotations/offers, purchase orders, call for tender documentation, procurement memo, contract, invoices, receipts, works/services completion certificates; Check the receiver’s ability to endorse payment;
In close coordination with the Admin Team, ensure that staff contracts are in line with standard salary grid, available budgets and regulations; propose salary grids revisions based on benchmarks, national legislation and budget constraint.
Validate partner’s accounting and documentation accuracy and compliance before payment.
Project budget follow-up, mission’s cost control, internal & external audits – anticipate and mitigate financial risks ensuring operations are run in a compliant and cost-efficient manner:
Lead Budget follow-ups, allocation and consolidation process;
Analyse/report gaps between planned budgets and actual expenses; comply to the flexibility rule;
Anticipate financial risks, present budget updates and mitigation plans to management;
Analyse and report monthly running costs, fleet and communication of each state office;
Prevent and report any financial and operational loss;
Follow-up with exiting staff to ensure they are cleared and validated;
Take the lead on external audit preparation in support to the compliance team; responses to audit reports, recommendations’ implementation plans.
Project Financial Cycle Management
Develop project budgets and reports – ensure the financial feasibility of projects, respecting internal and donors’ rules and deadlines;
Gather information from the relevant units to consolidate budgets for project proposals according to project needs and donor constraints;
Review and negotiate terms of grant contracts before signature (payment & financial reporting schedule, etc.);
